INSERT INTO tensor_maturity_verdicts (repo, scope, mission_id, level, evidence, verdict_by) VALUES ('TensorLBM', 'm15920 GAP-LBM-T2-GPU-COREPATH', 15939, 2, $json${"impl_files": "branch agent/m15920 commit ab74716d (not merged): src/tensorlbm/gpu_core_path.py 899 lines - collide_guo_into (BGK+Guo, :278-327), stream_into (:329-339), apply_channel_walls half-way bounce-back (:341-356), core_step (:358-375), GPUCorePathSolver (:433-630). main HEAD 123fe6b8 still ships the 718-line m15657 module, which raises AttributeError 'GPUCorePathConfig has no attribute perturbation_amplitude' at construction (artifacts/audit_m15939/evidence.json:main_module.probe_stdout) -> 0 of 4 delivered files merged", "entry": "python -m tensorlbm.gpu_core_path --ny 18 34 (module CLI, :876) + API run_channel_case(:727) / run_taylor_green_case(:798) / GPUCorePathSolver.step(:559)", "run_artifacts": "artifacts/t2_gpu_core_path/bench.json (mtime 05:02:02Z) + channel_profile.png/taylor_green_decay.png/channel_convergence.png + benchmarks/validation_matrix/cases/channel_core_path/result.json (04:56:45Z), all committed in ab74716d at 05:03:29Z = AFTER finished_at 2026-11-12 04:52:06Z; 0/2 on main; auditor re-ran the delivered entry in worktree m15939 and reproduced all 6 level x metric values with absolute difference 0.0 (evidence.json:audited_vs_rerun)", "tests": "tests/test_gpu_core_path.py 13 tests: 12 passed + 1 skipped in 49.08 s; the skipped one (test_compiled_backend_matches_eager) passes with TL_TEST_COMPILE=1 (1 passed, 11.05 s); file absent from main -> CI has no coverage", "integration_callers": "none in production code: only benchmarks/t2_gpu_core_path/bench.py:26 and benchmarks/validation_matrix/cases/channel_core_path/run.py:38 plus the matrix.json slot channel_core_path:593; no solver/Simulation/API imports gpu_core_path (git grep on HEAD and on ab74716d) -> L3 refused", "benchmark": "tensor_benchmark_cases rows for anchor GAP-LBM-T2-GPU-COREPATH = 0 (25-row table, no LBM T2 GPU row); tensorbench_results rows for m15920 = 0 -> no machine referee -> L4 refused. Measured anyway: profile rel L2 0.493% (ny=18) / 0.131% (ny=34) vs analytic Poiseuille, u_max 0.362%/0.099%, mass drift 4.9e-8/1.5e-6, Taylor-Green max KE err 1.27%/1.72% (nx=32), eager-vs-compiled rel field diff 2.33e-15/1.67e-15, speedup 3.78x/3.36x in the archived bench.json (4.14x in --quick), all CPU (no CUDA on host)", "repro_cmd": "TL_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 benchmarks/validation_matrix/cases/channel_core_path/run.py (83 s; metrics bit-identical to the audited result.json) ; TL_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 benchmarks/t2_gpu_core_path/bench.py --quick (119 s; 0.362%/0.493% @ny18, 4.14x, 2.33e-15) ; TL_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest tests/test_gpu_core_path.py -q (12 passed 1 skipped, 49 s)", "external_anchor": "analytic Poiseuille u(y)=a/(2 nu) s(H-s), s=y-0.5, H=ny-2, no-slip at y=0.5 and ny-1.5 (Batchelor 1967 ASFM 4.2; Ziegler 1993 half-way bounce-back; Ladd 1994); exact Taylor-Green decay E=u0^2/4 exp(-4 nu k^2 t) with k=2pi/nx (Taylor & Green 1937); Guo, Zheng & Shi PRE 65:046308 (2002) force scheme (both the u* shift and the discrete force term are implemented, :278-327). Auditor's own run with its own settings (check_every=500): profile L2 0.492%/0.126%, u_max 0.361%/0.094%, steady state verified before the step cap at both resolutions", "level_rationale": "L2, not L1: the deliverable is an executable solver with a public API and a CLI; the auditor reproduced input->compute->output through the delivered entry, and 13 tests assert invariants (mass conservation, streaming direction, half-way BB reflection, analytic Poiseuille/Taylor-Green, backend parity) rather than merely executing code. Not L3: zero callers in production code (only two bench drivers and a validation-matrix slot) and the whole deliverable is unmerged. Not L4: no tensor_benchmark_cases row and 0 tensorbench_results rows for the anchor, i.e. no machine referee, even though the 6 measured errors are all <=1.7% (inside the pre-existing 3% platform bar). Attached report size and 3 figures do not raise the level.", "overstated_claims": {"speedup": {"claimed": "4.15x", "artifact_of_record": "3.78x (ny=18) / 3.36x (ny=34)", "auditor_quick_run": "4.14x", "note": "claim reproducible only in --quick mode / best-of, not in the archived bench.json"}, "backend_parity": {"claimed": "3.3e-16", "measured": "max_abs_field_diff 7.77e-16/5.55e-16, rel 2.33e-15/1.67e-15", "note": "same order of machine epsilon; the quoted figure matches neither archived row"}, "tests": {"claimed": "13 items verified passing", "measured": "12 passed + 1 skipped; parity test needs TL_TEST_COMPILE=1", "note": "LOW"}, "precision_tier": {"claimed": "FP32FP16 store tier as a precision/performance trade-off (module docstring item 5)", "measured": "FP32FP16 == FP32FP32 to the last digit in bench.json; _f_store is written only by the 'f' property (:552-557), never inside _step_eager/_step_compiled", "note": "capability not exercised in the marching loop -> WITHHELD"}}, "findings": ["F1 BLOCKING: the deliverable never merged - ab74716d exists only on agent/m15920 (git merge-base --is-ancestor -> false); 0 of 4 delivered files carry m15920 content on main and 0 of 2 artifacts are on main, so the anchor's defect is still live on the platform: main's core path raises AttributeError 'perturbation_amplitude' on any legal config", "F2 MEDIUM: no tensor_benchmark_cases row for the anchor (0/25) and 0 tensorbench_results rows -> no machine referee -> L4 refused; the natural rows are already shaped by GAP-PP-6-run-artifacts (forward-Poiseuille profile, tol 3%)", "F3 MEDIUM: at mission close (04:52:06Z) the run_artifacts leg was empty - the mission said so honestly - and the artifacts were created 04:56-05:02Z by the still-running bench and committed by the auto-pusher at 05:03:29Z; they reproduce bit-identically, so the substance is real but the acceptance chain was closed out of band", "F4 MEDIUM: precision store tier is dead in the time loop (FP32FP16 metric row identical to FP32FP32, _f_store never written inside step) - the claimed precision/performance trade-off is not exercised", "F5 LOW: acceleration quoted as 4.15x while the artifact of record holds 3.78x/3.36x", "F6 LOW: '13 items passed' vs measured 12 passed + 1 skipped (compile-parity test is opt-in)", "F7 LOW: no CUDA on the audit host -> triton kernels, the Triton backend and DistributedGPUCorePathSolver halo exchange are unverified (bench multi_gpu status=not_run); the GPU half of 'GPU core path' is WITHHELD", "F8 LOW: the deliverable commit reindents benchmarks/validation_matrix/matrix.json wholesale (2-space -> 1-space, 1123 diff lines) - pure noise that raises merge-conflict surface"], "checks_not_run": ["no CUDA device on the audit host: Triton fused kernels, backend='triton', and the multi-GPU slab halo exchange were never executed (the two CUDA-only tests self-skip by design)", "the turbulent-channel intent of the m15657 config (re_tau/u_tau/Smagorinsky) was not exercised: main's module cannot even be constructed, and m15920's rewrite drops that configuration surface", "no cluster job was submitted for this audit (all legs are single-node, <= 2 min each; the full bench.json run takes 309 s on 1 thread)", "the 3 figures delivered by the mission were verified to exist and to be produced by bench.py but not re-derived from the JSON", "cross-host/cross-architecture (loong64 vs x86) reproducibility of the torch.compile parity was not varied"], "disposition": "approve L2 with notes; L3/L4 refused. Round-2 minimal actions: (a) merge ab74716d into main and let CI run tests/test_gpu_core_path.py (default + TL_TEST_COMPILE=1); (b) platform-side, register the anchor's tolerance rows (analytic-Poiseuille profile max/u_max at ny=18/34 plus Taylor-Green KE, 3% bar) so round 2 is machine-judgeable; (c) either wire the store dtype into the marching loop or drop the FP32FP16 claim. Until (a), GAP-LBM-T2-GPU-COREPATH must stay un-cleared on main.", "scope_note": "Audited m15920 (succeeded, accepted=true, no PR number, no merge commit; finished 2026-11-12 04:52:06Z) against main HEAD 123fe6b8 and its own branch tip ab74716d. Cross-checked: tensor_dev_missions row 15920 (result.checks/evidence/changed_files/headline), tensor_benchmark_cases (0 rows for the anchor of 25 total), tensorbench_results (0), git trees of ab74716d and HEAD, the audited work tree /root/tp-agent/work/m15920, and a full independent re-run of the delivered entry plus all 13 tests in /root/tp-agent/work/m15939."}$json$::jsonb, 'board-audit')
